From eebe1c7dd0811d8c992502f825fba7f4a6e8c94b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Hope <15705900+gabehope@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:55:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Hash kernels with integer arithmetic, and views without
 JSON

FpHash updated a BigInt polynomial per character (and per number) of what
it hashed, and AluExp.getHash() hashed a GlobalView's ShapeTracker as its
JSON string. Every eager operation builds and simplifies fresh expression
trees, so this ran on every dispatch; in an interactive plot it was
~60 ms of main-thread time per 16-move brush drag.

FpHash is now two 32-bit lanes of MurmurHash3-style mixing (Math.imul),
one word per value and per character pair, converted to a 64-bit bigint
once when read; `value` keeps its type. Views hash their shape, strides,
offset and mask directly (the fields JSON.stringify showed). Type tags
keep values of different types apart; -0 and 0 now hash differently.

Kernel construction (build and simplify) of a representative expression:
~85 us to ~46 us. Main-thread hashing in a brush drag: roughly halved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
